===========================================================
HST-CONSTRAINED MW–M31 MERGER SIMULATION STRATEGY
===========================================================

Project:
Constraining an N-body Milky Way–Andromeda merger simulation using
public HST proper motion measurements (van der Marel et al. 2012 and
subsequent updates).

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 1 — SCIENTIFIC GOAL
-----------------------------------------------------------
Objective:
Use observational constraints from HST to restrict the allowed
initial conditions of a Milky Way–M31 merger simulation, ensuring
that simulated present-day phase-space coordinates are consistent
with measured values.

Key idea:
Treat the simulation as a forward model and compare its outputs
(COM separation, velocities, angular momentum) against observations.

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 2 — OBSERVATIONAL DATA (HST)
-----------------------------------------------------------
Primary source:
van der Marel et al. 2012, ApJ 753, 8

Observed present-day quantities (with uncertainties):

1. Current separation:
   r_obs ≈ 770–780 kpc
   σ_r ≈ 20–30 kpc

2. Relative radial velocity:
   v_rad_obs ≈ −109 km/s
   σ_vrad ≈ 4 km/s

3. Relative tangential velocity:
   v_tan_obs ≈ 17 km/s
   σ_vtan ≈ 17 km/s

4. Inferred orbital angular momentum:
   Low, near-radial orbit

5. Total Local Group mass estimate:
   M_LG ≈ (2–3) × 10^12 M_sun

These values define the observational constraints the simulation
must reproduce at z ≈ 0.

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 3 — CONSTRAINED PARAMETERS IN THE CODE
-----------------------------------------------------------
Simulation parameters to be constrained:

- Initial MW–M31 separation vector r_0
- Initial relative velocity vector v_0
- Mass ratio (MW : M31)
- Halo scale lengths and concentrations (secondary constraint)

These are treated as free parameters within observational priors.

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 4 — PRIOR CONSTRUCTION
-----------------------------------------------------------
Define observational priors as probability distributions:

Separation prior:
  r_0 ~ Normal(r_obs, σ_r)

Radial velocity prior:
  v_rad_0 ~ Normal(v_rad_obs, σ_vrad)

Tangential velocity prior:
  v_tan_0 ~ Normal(v_tan_obs, σ_vtan)

Angular momentum prior:
  Implicitly enforced through v_tan distribution

These priors replace fixed initial conditions in the code.

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 5 — ENSEMBLE SIMULATION STRATEGY
-----------------------------------------------------------
Rationale:
Observational uncertainties imply a family of allowed orbits,
not a single deterministic trajectory.

Method:
- Sample N initial conditions from the priors (N ~ 100–1000)
- Run one full merger simulation per sample
- Store COM trajectories and snapshots

Each run is one realization of a plausible Local Group history.

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 6 — DIAGNOSTICS COMPUTED FROM EACH RUN
-----------------------------------------------------------
At each snapshot:

- Center-of-mass positions of MW and M31
- Relative separation:
  r_sim(t) = |r_M31(t) − r_MW(t)|

- Relative velocity:
  v_sim(t) = v_M31(t) − v_MW(t)

- Radial velocity:
  v_rad_sim = (r · v) / |r|

- Tangential velocity:
  v_tan_sim = sqrt(|v|^2 − v_rad_sim^2)

- Orbital angular momentum:
  L_orb = r × v

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 7 — COMPARISON WITH HST DATA
-----------------------------------------------------------
At the snapshot corresponding to “present day”:

Compute misfit metric:

χ² =
  ((r_sim − r_obs)/σ_r)^2
+ ((v_rad_sim − v_rad_obs)/σ_vrad)^2
+ ((v_tan_sim − v_tan_obs)/σ_vtan)^2

Interpretation:
Lower χ² indicates better agreement with HST measurements.

Optional likelihood formulation:
  L ∝ exp(−0.5 * χ²)

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 8 — SELECTION OF ACCEPTABLE SIMULATIONS
-----------------------------------------------------------
Procedure:
- Rank ensemble members by χ² or likelihood
- Select best-fitting subset (e.g., lowest 5–10%)

These runs define the HST-consistent parameter space.

Store:
- Initial conditions
- Merger times
- Orbital angular momentum histories
- Disk heating diagnostics

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 9 — VALIDATION CHECKS
-----------------------------------------------------------
Numerical validation:
- Energy conservation over time
- Angular momentum conservation (global)
- Sensitivity to timestep and softening length

Physical validation:
- Reasonable merger timescale (~4–6 Gyr)
- Near-radial infall consistent with low v_tan
- No unphysical disk disruption before pericenter

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 10 — SCIENTIFIC OUTPUTS
-----------------------------------------------------------
Primary results:
- Posterior distributions of initial velocities
- Allowed range of merger times
- Evolution of orbital angular momentum
- Predictions for disk heating and entropy growth

Deliverables:
- Tables of constrained parameters
- Trajectory plots (r(t), v_rad(t), v_tan(t))
- Diagnostics plots (energy, entropy, Lz)

-----------------------------------------------------------
ENTRY 11 — EXTENSIONS
-----------------------------------------------------------
Future improvements:
